PART 1 -- exact SU(2) one-plaquette spectrum = the group Laplacian on S^3
  class-angle form:  L f = -(1/sin^2 th) d/dth( sin^2 th f' ) ,  th in (0,pi)
  substitution f = u/sin(th)  =>  L = -u'' , u(0)=u(pi)=0
  => eigenvalues n^2-1 = 4j(j+1) = 3, 8, 15, 24, ...  (n = 2j+1)
  Verified below as a GENERALISED eigenproblem A f = lam B f, B = diag(sin^2 th).
