==============================================================================
PART 2 -- the read-only comparison, and why SU(2) has no scalar network
==============================================================================
  Geometric R_eff of the spatial 3-torus (the 'skeleton' of a 4D lattice,
  from qg1 PART A):  L=4: 0.4333,  L=6: 0.4539,  L=8: 0.46595
  It SATURATES (R_inf ~ 0.47): it is L-independent, and beta-independent.

  Read-only corpus numbers at beta = 2.5 (SU(2), 4D):
     m_1 a = 1/(xi/a) in [0.77, 1.89]         (BN-RESIDUAL.md:293)
     strong-coupling first term m a = 1.88    (same line)
     m_{0++*}/m_{0++} ~ 1.54-1.56             (AUDIT-CH16.md:33)

  Multiplying by the geometric R_eff ~ 0.47 gives 0.36-0.89: bounded, and
  L-independent BECAUSE R_eff is L-independent and m a is L-independent.
  The same test on free Maxwell gives  w_min*R_eff ~ 1/L -> 0 (qg3 ACID 1).

  So the test does separate gapped from gapless -- but only because it is
  literally 'is lambda L-independent?' with a beta-free constant stuck on.
  All the discriminating information sits in lambda, none in R_eff.

  WHY THERE IS NO SCALAR NETWORK (T0b, sharp):
   (i) For a scalar network the Dirichlet form is E(f)=sum_e c_e (f_x-f_y)^2,
       i.e. a QUADRATIC form in the vertex variables.  The Wilson weight
       exp(beta Re tr U_p) is NOT a quadratic form in the link variables:
       it is a matrix element of the regular representation, and the
       quadratic expansion around a background is the Savvidy Hessian
       -D^2 + 2 ad F_B -- an OPERATOR in the adjoint fibre, indefinite.
   (ii) A conductance is a positive number.  'ad F_B' has both signs, so the
       'conductances' of any non-abelian effective network are sign-indefinite
       => no M-matrix => no effective resistance (R_eff is defined only for
       PSD Laplacians with non-negative weights).
   (iii) Even the abelian Z2 case works only because U(1)/Z_N plaquettes
       exponentiate to a real positive weight after the duality transform;
       for SU(2) the dual is not a spin model with positive weights.
  => the constant c in lambda >= c/R_eff would have to carry a g-dependence
     (T0b), and the monotonicity direction (T0c) has no meaning.

